      "side": 1,
      "message": "Summarizing out-of-band discussion with Eric:\n\u003e PD 3.0, section 5.8.6 contains the requirements for detecting non-idle. The receiver must detect nTransitionCount transitions within tTransitionWindow, where nTransitionCount is at least 3, and tTransitionWindow is 12-20 us. Although no maximum is listed for nTransitionCount, an arbitrarily high value would prevent any non-idle detection. It seems reasonable to interpret Table 5-19 to mean that nTransitionCount should be 3.\n\n\u003e The default behavior of the RT1715 sets nTransitionCount \u003d 3 (CTRL1[TRANSCNT]) and tTransitionWindow \u003d 46.67 us (unnamed register at 0x82). This value of tTransitionWindow is non-compliant.\n\n\u003e This CL changes nTransitionCount to 7 and leaves tTransitionWindow at 46.67 us, approximately doubling the threshold for non-idle detection within this approximately double-spec-size window.\n\nFor improving noise rejection, would it be as effective to leave nTransitionCount \u003d 3 and set tTransitionWindow to 20 us? That seems like a more compliant solution.\n\nIf this discussion is non-trivial, we can revisit it in a future CL. I\u0027m OK with finishing up this one, because it seems to improve test results.",
      "revId": "e4381fe356e6ddc86ff05f2bac08a576d38aa218",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
